---
import ServiceLayout from '../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<ServiceLayout
  title="Pipe Locating Services"
  description={`Pipe locating in Asheville & Hendersonville, NC: find buried water and sewer lines before you dig, build or repair. Call Nesbitt's Plumbing at ${site.phone}.`}
  heroTitle="Pipe Locating Services"
  heroSubtitle="Know exactly where your buried water and sewer lines run before anyone starts digging in Asheville, Hendersonville, NC and the surrounding areas."
  heroImage="/images/gallery/gallery-21.jpg"
  listHeading="When to Call for Pipe Locating:"
  listItems={[
    'Before digging for an addition, deck, fence, pool or driveway',
    'Finding a leak or break on a buried water line',
    'Locating a sewer line, cleanout or septic connection',
    'Planning a water or sewer line replacement',
    'Older properties with no record of where lines were run',
  ]}
  listNote="Pair pipe locating with a video inspection to see the condition of your sewer line, not just where it is."
  ctaHeading="Need to Find a Buried Line?"
  photosHeading="Water & Sewer Line Work"
  photos={[
    { src: '/images/gallery/gallery-21.jpg', alt: 'Plumber working on buried pipes in a trench in Asheville, NC', caption: 'Trench work on buried lines' },
    { src: '/images/gallery/gallery-03.jpg', alt: 'Sewer line repair and replacement in Asheville, NC', caption: 'Sewer line repair/replacement' },
    { src: '/images/gallery/excavator-pipe-removal.jpg', alt: 'Excavator removing an old corrugated pipe in Western North Carolina', caption: 'Digging out an old failed pipe' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-charcoal-900 sm:text-3xl">Find It Before You Dig</h2>
  <p>
    Digging blind is how water lines get cut and sewer lines get crushed. Nesbitt's Plumbing
    locates buried water and sewer lines on your property so you know where they run before work
    begins, whether you're planning a project or trying to track down a problem.
  </p>
  <p>
    Public utility lines are marked for free through NC 811, but private lines on your side of the
    meter usually aren't: the water line to your house, your sewer lateral, or lines out to a
    garage, barn or second building. That's where we come in. Once a line is found, we can mark it,
    repair it, or replace it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Call <a href={site.phoneHref} class="font-semibold text-drop-600 hover:underline">{site.phone}</a>
    to schedule pipe locating.
  </p>
</ServiceLayout>
